{
  "requirement": "A GitHub Actions CI workflow MUST run, for pull requests and pushes to `main`, these checks: `cargo habeas coverage -- --locked --workspace` under {cite}`requirements.test-coverage.run`, `cargo test --locked --doc --workspace`, `mdbook test`, the autofix controller tests with `node --test .github/scripts/autofix.test.mjs`, and, in a separate job, the Symposium session-start hook smoke test `tests/symposium_hook_smoke.py`. It also builds the book as documentation under {cite}`requirements.index.render_only`, without requiring collected execution reports for rendering. On a push to `main`, only after every check job passes, it deploys the generated `book/` directory to GitHub Pages. The book MUST set `output.html.site-url` to `/habeas-codicem/` for project-site hosting.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The single marked test, `tests/repository.rs#fn[ci_tests_pull_requests_and_main_then_deploys_the_book_from_main]`, covers each testable obligation in `requirements.integration.ci`.\n\n- **Triggers:** it asserts the exact `on:` block, with `push` limited to `branches: [main]` plus `pull_request`.\n- **Check steps:** it scopes to the `test-and-build` job via `workflow_job` and finds these steps in order:\n  - `node --test .github/scripts/autofix.test.mjs`\n  - `cargo habeas coverage -- --locked --workspace`\n  - `cargo test --locked --doc --workspace`\n  - `mdbook test`\n  - `mdbook build`\n  - the Pages artifact upload with `path: book`\n- **Coverage gate:** it asserts the `coverage-check` step has no `if` and no `continue-on-error`. The requirement doesn't name this step, so this is extra.\n- **Hook smoke test:** it asserts that the separate `symposium-hook` job runs `python3 tests/symposium_hook_smoke.py`.\n- **Deploy:** it asserts the `deploy` job has `if: github.event_name == 'push' && github.ref == 'refs/heads/main'` and `needs: [test-and-build, symposium-hook]`. It also asserts the job uses `actions/deploy-pages@v4`. Together these cover deploying only on a push to `main`, and only after every check job passes.\n- **Site URL:** it asserts `book.toml` `output.habeas.html.site-url` equals `/habeas-codicem/`. The book uses a custom `habeas` renderer, so this is the HTML output table that carries `site-url`.\n\nThe clause \"builds the book as documentation ... without requiring collected execution reports\" has no workflow-level assertion. The test does assert that an `mdbook build` step exists. That clause is about what `habeas mdbook` does, which `requirements.index.render_only` governs. That requirement is cited, not subject to reassessment here. The workflow offers nothing else to check for it, so I count no gap.\n\nThe assertions are substring and position checks. Plausible violations such as a missing job, a wrong trigger, a missing `needs`, a wrong deploy condition, or a wrong `site-url` would each fail them.",
  "references": "a8abf153c89272233a77553f9d744b8b6c5dbba98424eae9956c0f6b77735200",
